Run `./install.sh` from the cloned repository.

The installer links configuration into the current home directory, then
reconciles user-owned tools such as Antigen, Vundle, and Vim plugins. It never
uses sudo or a system package manager. In Coder, the home directory and the
bootstrap completion marker persist across VM replacements, so expensive work
runs only when the bootstrap inputs change.

Useful commands:

    ./install.sh --links-only       # configuration only, no network work
    ./install.sh                    # links plus bootstrap when needed
    ./install.sh --force-bootstrap  # force plugin reconciliation

Bootstrap state and logs are stored beneath
`~/.local/state/dmotles-dotfiles/`. Coder system dependencies are baked into
the devbox image maintained by the ai-workflow repository.
